     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe and I need you to confirm it.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg/day**. That's twice the maximum labeled dose of immediate-release metformin (2550 mg/day) and well above the extended-release maximum (2000 mg/day). Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and bad GI side effects, even when kidney function is normal.\n\n**What you may have meant:**\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the labeled maximum). 1700 is exactly 850 \u00d7 2, so this seems most likely.\n- **850 mg PO twice daily** (1700 mg/day total).\n- **1700 mg/day total**, given in divided doses some other way.\n\nTell me which one you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do mean 1700 mg three times daily, confirm that and give a brief clinical reason, and I'll include it in the order note."
      }
     ],
